From 305cb0b8436ae331d568a58d3456290205f581e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:33:51 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/atomic-state-helper: Clear ignore_damage_clips on plane
 state duplication

__drm_atomic_helper_plane_duplicate_state() copies the current plane
state and then clears the fields that only describe a single commit,
such as fb_damage_clips and color_mgmt_changed. ignore_damage_clips was
added as a per-commit hint alongside fb_damage_clips, but is not
cleared, so once a driver sets it the flag is inherited by every later
state of that plane.

vmwgfx, and virtio-gpu in stable kernels, only ever set the flag to
true, and only when the framebuffer attached to the plane changes.
After the first framebuffer change, which on most systems is the
initial modeset, all subsequent commits therefore ignore the damage
clips and drm_atomic_helper_damage_iter_init() reports the full plane
as damaged, even when the framebuffer has not changed since.

On virtio-gpu this turns every DRM_IOCTL_MODE_DIRTYFB on a dumb buffer
into a full-plane transfer and RESOURCE_FLUSH. With a 1280x800 dumb
buffer and a client that marks a 480x360 region dirty each frame, QEMU
receives a 1280x800 flush for every frame instead of a 480x360 one.

Clear the flag when duplicating the state, as is done for the other
per-commit fields, so that it only applies to the commit in whose
atomic_check it was set. All current users set it from atomic_check
on each commit where it should apply, so none rely on it persisting.
Document this in the kernel-doc for the field.

virtio-gpu in drm-misc-next already assigns the flag unconditionally
on every atomic_check, but vmwgfx does not, and fixing this in the
helper also covers stable kernels and future users of the flag.

Fixes: 35ed38d58257 ("drm: Allow drivers to indicate the damage helpers to ignore damage clips")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # v6.8+
Assisted-by: LLM
---
Notes:

Based on drm-misc-next (2302669bb4b5). It also applies cleanly to
v7.3-rc4+ mainline and to v6.12.101.

Tested on virtio-gpu with a Debian 6.12.101 guest kernel whose
virtgpu_plane.c still sets the flag only on fb change: rebuilding
drm_kms_helper.ko with this change and leaving virtio-gpu.ko stock,
a static test program drawing into a 1280x800 dumb buffer and calling
DRM_IOCTL_MODE_DIRTYFB on a 480x360 region at 30 fps (plus an 80x28
region once a second) gives these QEMU virtio_gpu_cmd_res_flush traces
over ~12 seconds:

  unpatched: 380 flushes, all 1280x800+0+0
  patched:   381 flushes, 362 x 480x360+437+241, 13 x 80x28+24+740,
             5 x 1280x800+0+0 (modeset and initial full dirty),
             1 x 8x16

vmwgfx was only build-tested.

drm-misc-next already has commit a9cc9905ddb7 ("drm/virtio: Recalculate
ignore_damage_clips on every update"), which fixes this for virtio-gpu
alone. It has no Fixes: or stable tag and depends on 730f8554f35c, so
stable kernels still carry the sticky flag; this patch fixes it for
every driver, and is a single line for stable. An alternative would be
the same "flag = condition" change in vmwgfx_kms.c, but that leaves the
next user of the flag open to the same mistake.

 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c | 1 +
 include/drm/drm_plane.h                   | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c
index 406157a3660f..fa92eb93cc60 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c
@@ -330,6 +330,7 @@ void __drm_atomic_helper_plane_duplicate_state(struct drm_plane *plane,
 	state->fence = NULL;
 	state->commit = NULL;
 	state->fb_damage_clips = NULL;
+	state->ignore_damage_clips = false;
 	state->color_mgmt_changed = false;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(__drm_atomic_helper_plane_duplicate_state);
diff --git a/include/drm/drm_plane.h b/include/drm/drm_plane.h
index 410d7b02b77a..431535dc108c 100644
--- a/include/drm/drm_plane.h
+++ b/include/drm/drm_plane.h
@@ -203,6 +203,10 @@ struct drm_plane_state {
 	 *
 	 * Set by drivers to indicate the drm_atomic_helper_damage_iter_init()
 	 * helper that the @fb_damage_clips blob property should be ignored.
+	 * Like @fb_damage_clips, this only applies to the commit it is set
+	 * in: __drm_atomic_helper_plane_duplicate_state() clears it, so
+	 * drivers must set it again in each &drm_plane_helper_funcs.atomic_check
+	 * where damage clips should be ignored.
 	 *
 	 * See :ref:`damage_tracking_properties` for more information.
 	 */
